# Sample requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start the API first: ./demo/run.sh

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### --- Task 1: core endpoints ---

### Create a deposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "amount": 500,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "deposit"
}

### Create a transfer
# @name createTransfer
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "transfer"
}

### Create a withdrawal that exceeds the balance -> status "failed"
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": 999999,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "withdrawal"
}

### List all transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions

### Get the transfer created above by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{createTransfer.response.body.id}}

### Unknown transaction -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/does-not-exist

### Account balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-12345/balance

### --- Task 2: validation ---

### Several invalid fields at once -> 400 with details
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-1",
  "toAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": -10.555,
  "currency": "XYZ",
  "type": "transfer"
}

### Too many decimal places -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "amount": 10.999,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "type": "deposit"
}

### --- Task 3: filtering ---

### By account
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345

### By type
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=transfer

### By date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?from=2024-01-01&to=2024-01-31

### Combined
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345&type=deposit&from=2024-01-01&to=2024-01-31

### Invalid filter -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=refund

### --- Task 4: additional features ---

### Option A: account summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-12345/summary

### Option B: simple interest (5% annual rate, 30 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-12345/interest?rate=0.05&days=30

### Option C: CSV export (accepts the same filters as GET /transactions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv&accountId=ACC-12345

### Option D: rate limiting - see the X-RateLimit-* response headers.
# Run demo/sample-requests.sh rate-limit to exceed 100 requests/minute and get 429.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
